[[:db/retract 17592186085515 :answer-field/choices 17592186085517] [:db/retract 17592186085515 :answer-field/choices 17592186085518] [:db/retract 17592186085515 :answer-field/choices 17592186085519] [:db/retract 17592186085509 :answer-field/choices 17592186085510] [:db/retract 17592186085509 :answer-field/choices 17592186085511] [:db/retract 17592186085509 :answer-field/choices 17592186085512] [:db/retract 17592186085509 :answer-field/choices 17592186085513] [:db/retract 17592186085509 :answer-field/choices 17592186085514] {:db/id 17592186087877 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087878 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087879 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454" :question/id #uuid "73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454" :question/math-academy-id "q-335274" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=2x$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2x\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}}) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97ed5649-7d28-5597-8785-b502fbbd5161" "answer-0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" "answer-39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" "answer-a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" "answer-1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97ed5649-7d28-5597-8785-b502fbbd5161" :answer/id #uuid "97ed5649-7d28-5597-8785-b502fbbd5161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" :answer/id #uuid "0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" :answer/id #uuid "39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/id #uuid "a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}})={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d" :answer/id #uuid "1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" :question/id #uuid "536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339139" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=5.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 5 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={x}^{5}+C \\\\ y & =x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" "answer-field-658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" :answer-field/id #uuid "054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" "answer-f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" "answer-8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" "answer-21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" :answer/id #uuid "cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" :answer/id #uuid "f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" :answer/id #uuid "8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997" :answer-field/id #uuid "658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" "answer-a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" "answer-856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" "answer-96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" :answer/id #uuid "cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" :answer/id #uuid "a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1" :answer/id #uuid "96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311587 :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088144 :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot y=x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =\\int 2{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/4} \\\\ 1 & =2+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186085515 :answer-field/correct "answer-8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae550e0c-1776-5b97-ab81-e46cb204df85" "answer-8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" "answer-fc50ddf9-0597-5079-a434-4f4d589089a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae550e0c-1776-5b97-ab81-e46cb204df85" :answer/id #uuid "ae550e0c-1776-5b97-ab81-e46cb204df85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/id #uuid "8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc50ddf9-0597-5079-a434-4f4d589089a3" :answer/id #uuid "fc50ddf9-0597-5079-a434-4f4d589089a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186085509 :answer-field/correct "answer-e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" "answer-d15343f4-d7a9-5b07-861f-21158d88cd11" "answer-42485b83-5931-53b1-8e35-f51001ba1f8e" "answer-f6d4fe97-8780-56b9-9818-a1be81f11d20" "answer-9ffccaf5-41e6-5e01-a737-ef5c5c68550a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer/id #uuid "e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d15343f4-d7a9-5b07-861f-21158d88cd11" :answer/id #uuid "d15343f4-d7a9-5b07-861f-21158d88cd11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42485b83-5931-53b1-8e35-f51001ba1f8e" :answer/id #uuid "42485b83-5931-53b1-8e35-f51001ba1f8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6d4fe97-8780-56b9-9818-a1be81f11d20" :answer/id #uuid "f6d4fe97-8780-56b9-9818-a1be81f11d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ffccaf5-41e6-5e01-a737-ef5c5c68550a" :answer/id #uuid "9ffccaf5-41e6-5e01-a737-ef5c5c68550a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858" :question/id #uuid "eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858" :question/math-academy-id "q-335830" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-2x} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & ={e}^{2x}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={e}^{2(0)}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 4 & =C-1 \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" "answer-field-872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" :answer-field/id #uuid "db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" "answer-b2373707-12f6-5094-9104-60d956b3f32f" "answer-0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" "answer-89b946b2-2ff0-52e9-9809-36bbebc85401"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" :answer/id #uuid "12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2373707-12f6-5094-9104-60d956b3f32f" :answer/id #uuid "b2373707-12f6-5094-9104-60d956b3f32f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/id #uuid "0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89b946b2-2ff0-52e9-9809-36bbebc85401" :answer/id #uuid "89b946b2-2ff0-52e9-9809-36bbebc85401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390" :answer-field/id #uuid "872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" "answer-f1b016d8-b939-5406-bcfa-caab3f97d6bf" "answer-1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" "answer-cf7b3997-dd21-54f1-8bae-4ea74ec54405" "answer-ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" :answer/id #uuid "21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-2x}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1b016d8-b939-5406-bcfa-caab3f97d6bf" :answer/id #uuid "f1b016d8-b939-5406-bcfa-caab3f97d6bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" :answer/id #uuid "1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}(1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf7b3997-dd21-54f1-8bae-4ea74ec54405" :answer/id #uuid "cf7b3997-dd21-54f1-8bae-4ea74ec54405" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(3+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/id #uuid "ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088861 :tutorial/content "We will now derive the formula for the integrating factor. \n\nConsider the first-order linear equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x).\n$$\n\nOur goal is to rewrite the left-hand side as the derivative of a product.\n\nTo do that, we multiply both sides of the equation by some function $I(x)$ that we wish to determine.\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}I(x)\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + {\\color{purple}I(x)P(x)}y} = I(x)Q(x)\n$$\n\nWe want the left-hand side to match the derivative of $y\\cdot I(x)$. But by the product rule,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Bigl(y\\cdot I(x)\\Bigr)\n=\n{\\color{blue}I(x)\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + {\\color{purple}I'(x)}y}.\n$$\n\nSo, if we choose $I(x)$ so that\n\n$$\nI'(x) = I(x)P(x),\n$$\n\nthen the left-hand side becomes $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Bigl(y\\cdot I(x)\\Bigr).$\n\nDividing both sides of $I'(x) = I(x)P(x)$ by $I(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{I'(x)}{I(x)} = P(x).\n$$\n\nNext, integrating both sides with respect to $x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{I}^{′}(x)}{I(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(I(x)))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(I(x)) & =\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x+C \\\\ I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x+C} \\\\  & ={e}^{C}\\cdot {e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, because multiplying $I(x)$ by a nonzero constant does not change the method, we can choose $e^C = 1$ and define an integrating factor as\n\n$$\nI(x) = e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087942 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
